  "premise": "Wren Zhou has spent twelve years keeping their online identity sealed away from their real life — until notes begin appearing in their school locker, written by the legendary ghost of Hollowmere High, addressed to Wren by a name no one should know, in ink that glows and vanishes. As Wren investigates, they discover the ghost is not dead but hiding: a former student, Juniper, who has been living inside the school's forgotten sub-basement for a decade, protected by a found family of misfits who each keep one piece of her secret. When the school board moves to demolish the building — and with it, Juniper's refuge and life — Wren must choose between the loyalty of the friends who trusted them with the secret and the truth that could save Juniper but expose everyone. In the end, Wren tells the truth, the found family fractures and reforms around a new pact, and Juniper steps into the daylight for the first time in ten years as the school, saved by public outcry, is converted into a community archive with a hidden room no one ever needs again.",
